From 2cbfac3d0987b943bd441367d3c62358f0a7b6b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liu Dongmiao <473522+liudongmiao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:08:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] quic: resend unacknowledged STREAM data in 1-RTT PTO probes

A 1-RTT PTO probe carried only PING when no new data was pending, so
lost STREAM data was not resent until an ACK showed it lost. If every
such ACK was lost too, a request could stay unsent.

When no stream has data it can send now, pick the lowest-ID stream with
sent data or a sent FIN still unacknowledged. Requeue its first
unacknowledged data, as much as fits in the probe, or its FIN alone.

Add quic_txp_test scripts for 1-RTT probes resending data and a FIN,
and for streams that have data but cannot send it now.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
